atorname{arccos}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9091/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e89b620-641a-5dbf-85f6-ca0f7a2fad80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9091"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-24763/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "12382967-86bd-5b41-a29f-37c1efe1b9d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24763/selection/8054304fddf4b48693ad35887faf99224ec7548e30e7afaf6bf777ee8da45450" :answer/id #uuid "ea8486dc-b3e6-5c77-9137-d9ee33632c56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24763/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "d698581f-9f3e-5d93-b736-7c0b543331cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24763/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" :answer/id #uuid "6b3fb63f-08fc-5ab6-a842-80fa6cf2a7a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24763/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "43553a