/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({315}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${315}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${315}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{315}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =2\\cdot (-{45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-{90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117408/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117408"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117459/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "b08c59d8-1d5f-5f8a-8d6f-811893576822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117459/selection/f9d7239105cd67d6f6d6cd6caa594063c6cfce814e0c4df6a21699bcb39f6159" :answer/id #uuid "76c0fca7-dff2-5d5a-96dd-83e54c96fc4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{270}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117459/selection/4fea3101a12d72027d37d2702205342eaae6c8b446484d84e77543a2510dec4d" :answer/id #uuid "47397b00-304a-5df6-a597-8b9111eecb31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117459/selection/494cd77ad8a9b447737f156e4d1a6455198b704f906ab2283374911afa938361" :answer/id #uuid "990ce949-4c0a-5924-bce5-139a020c9764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117459/selection/fdad1f8a9ae245b85e8d